-- Zero-K counter matrix, flattened.
--
-- One value per ordered unit pair: what the pick is worth against that target.
-- 1.00 is even, above is a counter, below is being counter-picked. There are no
-- layers and no blending -- gui_build_proposer.lua reads this number and uses it.
--
-- Generated from the counter matrix editor on 2026-09-06.
-- 368 pairings re-tuned in the editor on 2026-09-10 and applied here.
-- 334 pairings re-tuned in the editor on 2026-09-11 and applied here.
-- 384 pairings re-tuned in the editor on 2026-09-12 and applied here.
-- Hand-edited values were made in the editor; everything else was resolved out of
-- the old three-layer matrix (named pair > unit-vs-archetype > archetype row) at the
-- moment of flattening. The layered original, with all of its sourcing comments, is
-- kept beside this file in gui_build_proposer_layers_archive.lua.
--
-- Keys starting with "#" are the fallback columns, used whenever the target is not
-- named by the row being read: unlisted buildings, chickens, drones, any unit added
-- after this file was generated, and every commander. "#defense" is any armed
-- building, "#eco" any unarmed one; the rest are the unit classes.
--
-- Commanders have five rows of their own, one per chassis, with full pairings like any
-- other unit. The widget maps every commander unitDef onto one of those five names, so
-- "#commander" is only reached for a chassis this table has never heard of.

